; surface form — the inflected or derived form of a stem under a vachana
; produced by applying a vachana (eka/dvi/bahu) to a dhatu
; A rupa B means B is the surface form of stem A
; antisymmetric: surface form is not its own stem

(sangati rupa
  (sthita bhasha-swarupa)
  (yukta dhatu)
  (janya vachana))
